                <pb facs="0481" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2783</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-25T11:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1918, 11 a.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 25, 10.35
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. Yesterday agreement was made between Siberian government and Horvat, latter to be a member of Siberian
                    government and to act as its general commissioner for Far East with authority of
                    civil governor general. This followed immediately after arrival here of
                        Vologodski, head of Omsk Siberian
                    government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
